# A deliberately small magic database for the console's `file` command.
#
# file(1)'s own database is 10.8 MB and libmagic reads all of it into memory
# on magic_load(); that is far too much to ship with a web page.  These are
# the formats that can actually appear in this filesystem -- what the seed
# tree contains, what apt/apt-get download, and what a user can create with
# base64, curl or a heredoc.  Everything else is still recognised, because
# text, JSON, CSV, tar and ELF detection live in libmagic's own code
# (ascmagic.c, is_json.c, is_csv.c, is_tar.c, readelf.c), not in this file.
#
# Recompile after editing:
#   node tools/gen_magicmgc.js assets/libmagic.js . src/magicmgc.data.js data/magic

